35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"The survey shows daylight was the top complaint, yet the plan gives only four desks windows. That feels unfair to the three on the wall.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The badge data confirms first-come, first-served is broken. Half the team arrives after ten. We cannot rely on arrival time to assign seats.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, that confirms my worry. We are billed for area, not people. Two empty desks cost us 41,000 yen monthly.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mio,,"@Daisuke, that’s a lot of money for empty space. But my findings show mornings take four to nine minutes, and shuffles last two weeks.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Nine decibels louder by the printer, and my chair takes days to settle. That’s not comfort, that’s a daily tax.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, those two weeks of shuffles sound exhausting. @Shunichi, I understand the noise is a real burden.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shizue, the plan is lopsided. Four get windows, three get walls. We must decide who takes the worse end deliberately, not by habit.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Mio, the 6,200 yen per desk fee for re-running power and network is also a recurring cost. Every change adds up.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, two weeks of chaos is unacceptable. @Daisuke, that recurring fee makes me nervous. We need a layout that stops the constant moving.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Toshio, deliberate is better than habit. But if I pick the quiet window, I lose my settled chair. That’s a trade-off, not a free lunch.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Toshio, you are right. We must be fair. @Shunichi, your comfort matters too. Let us find a balance that respects everyone’s needs.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, the trade-off is real. But the badge data proves first-come is broken. We need a system that ignores arrival time entirely.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, I agree. If we change seats often, the 6,200 yen fee hits us every time. We need a stable plan to save money.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, I agree. Stability saves time and money. @Daisuke, those fees are scary. We need a layout that stays put.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Toshio, ignoring arrival time is smart. But stability means my chair settles. I need a fixed spot to avoid that daily tax.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Toshio, I agree. We must be deliberate. @Shunichi, your comfort is valid. Let us find a balance that respects everyone’s needs.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, stability is the only way to avoid the recurring fees. We must choose a system that assigns seats deliberately, not by chance.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Toshio, I agree. Stability saves the 61,000 yen monthly. We must avoid the recurring 6,200 yen fees.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@Toshio, I agree. Stability is key. If we keep moving, I lose those precious gaps. Let’s pick a layout that stays put.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Toshio, agreed. A fixed spot lets my chair settle and keeps me away from the noise. Stability is the only rational choice here.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
